## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design per-tenant privacy controls in a real-world multi-tenant GCP SaaS, balancing performance, data isolation, and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time data redaction with Cloud DLP integrated into Dataflow pipelines
- Per-tenant Cloud Storage buckets and BigQuery datasets with CMEK-managed encryption
- IAM Conditions for tenant-scoped least-privilege access controls
- Synthetic-tenant CI validation with automated rollback on policy violations

## Code Example
```terraform
# Per-tenant IAM condition binding
resource "google_project_iam_binding" "tenant_access" {
  project = var.project_id
  role    = "roles/storage.objectViewer"
  members = ["serviceAccount:${var.analyst_sa}"]
  condition {
    title       = "tenant_isolation_${var.tenant_id}"
    description = "Restrict access to tenant ${var.tenant_id} data only"
    expression  = "resource.labels.tenant_id == '${var.tenant_id}'"
  }
}

# Per-tenant Cloud Storage bucket with CMEK
resource "google_storage_bucket" "tenant_bucket" {
  name     = "${var.project_id}-data-${var.tenant_id}"
  location = var.region
  encryption {
    default_kms_key_name = google_kms_crypto_key.tenant_key.id
  }
  labels = {
    tenant_id = var.tenant_id
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates expertise in designing tenant-isolated logging architectures—a critical security requirement in multi-tenant SaaS platforms where log exposure can lead to data breaches.

## Key Concepts
- Cloud Logging Router with tenant-specific sinks using label-based filtering
- IAM Conditions implementing least-privilege access controls
- Data Loss Prevention API for automatic PII redaction
- CI/CD pipeline integration with synthetic tenant provisioning
- Automated rollback mechanisms for isolation verification

## Code Example
```javascript
// Conceptual tenant sink configuration
const tenantSink = {
  name: `tenant-${tenantId}-sink`,
  filter: `resource.type="cloud_run_revision" AND labels.tenant_id="${tenantId}"`,
  destination: `bigquery.googleapis.com/projects/${projectId}/datasets/tenant_${tenantId}_logs`
};

// IAM Condition for tenant access
const tenantAccessCondition = {
  title: `Tenant ${tenantId} Log Access`,
  expression: `resource.name.startsWith("projects/${projectId}/datasets/tenant_${tenantId}_")`
};
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical, concrete incident response steps for a multi-tenant GCP SaaS, focusing on rapid containment, credential revocation, and rollback with auditable forensics.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation and containment
- Workload Identity and bindings management
- Network controls: NetworkPolicy, Private Service Connect, VPC Service Controls
- Forensics preservation and rollback playbooks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: containment workflow
const onExfiltration = () => {
  isolateTenant();
  revokeIdentity();
  blockEgress();
  preserveForensics();
  runSyntheticTests();
  rollbackIfNeeded();
}
```

